# Architecture (expense-tracker-mobile)

This app is **Vite + React 18 + shadcn/ui + Tailwind + Redux Toolkit**, not the legacy MUI frontend. Follow the layers below.

## Layer map

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Shell | `src/app/` | Routes, guards, providers, search |
| Features | `src/features/{name}/` | Screens and feature-scoped UI |
| Domain | `src/domain/{entity}/` | `{entity}.model.js`, `*.rules.js`, `*.validators.js`, `*.transformers.js` |
| Infrastructure | `src/infrastructure/` | `api/`, `demo/`, `cache/`, `websocket/` |
| Redux | `src/redux/` | Per-slice `*.actions.js`, `*.reducer.js`, `*.actionTypes.js`, `store.js` |
| Shared | `src/shared/` | `components/`, `hooks/`, `patterns/`, `utils/`, `contracts/` |
| UI primitives | `src/components/ui/` | shadcn/Radix primitives only |
| Config | `src/config/` | `runtime/`, `theme/`, `navigation/`, `chart/`, `api/`, `auth/`, `ui/` |
| i18n | `src/i18n/` | `LanguageContext.jsx`, `translations/en.js`, `hi.js`, `te.js` |
| Styles | `src/styles/` | `globals.css` |

## Feature folder contract

Every `src/features/{name}/` must include:

- `pages/` — route-level pages only (one primary export per file; filename matches export). Keep **flat** unless several routes clearly belong in a sub-route group (rare).
- `components/` — feature-only UI, organized by **concern subfolders** (see below).
- `hooks/` — feature-scoped hooks (`use*.js` only), organized by **concern subfolders** when the feature grows (see below).

Optional: `config/`, `constants/`, `utils/`, `context/`, `validation/`. Optional nested folders under `utils/` (e.g. `utils/reports/`) when many helpers share a domain.

Use **kebab-case** for multi-word feature folders (`payment-methods`, `grouped-report-accordion`).

### `components/` subfolders

Do **not** leave large flat piles of files in `components/`. Group files into **one concern per folder**, using additional levels when a concern splits further (e.g. `components/reports/panels/` only if justified by file count).

Standard concern names (pick what applies; omit empty folders):

| Subfolder | Holds |
|-----------|--------|
| `form/` | Form fields, field groups, form shells, autocompletes tied to the feature form |
| `list/` | List rows, cards in list context, list toolbars |
| `overview/` | Summary strips, stat cards, high-level non-chart summaries |
| `charts/` | Chart widgets and chart-only cards |
| `filters/` | Filter bars, filter sheets, popovers whose job is filtering |
| `reports/` | Report layout sections, headers, export UI tied to reporting |
| `export/` | Dedicated export menus or dialogs |
| `dialogs/` | Feature modals/dialogs not covered elsewhere |
| `accordion/` | Accordion-specific building blocks |
| `table/` | Table-specific rows, summaries |
| `sections/` | Page sections in settings-like UIs |
| `common/` | Small shared pieces used only inside this feature’s components |
| `budget/` | Budget-specific UI when the feature mixes budget + other flows |

Rules:

- Add a subfolder when **multiple files** share the same concern or when the plan already names a category.
- **Feature root** `components/index.js` may re-export public symbols; prefer `@/features/{name}/components/` imports for consumers outside the feature.
- **Nested subfolders** inside a concern are allowed when the folder would otherwise exceed a manageable handful of files.

### `hooks/` subfolders

Only files named **`use*.js`** (or `use*.jsx` if unavoidable). No pure helpers in `hooks/` — those belong in `utils/`.

Group hooks by **domain concern**, mirroring `components/` where it helps:

| Subfolder (examples) | Typical hooks |
|------------------------|---------------|
| `form/` | `useExpenseForm`, `useBillForm` |
| `list/` | `useExpenseList`, `useBillList` |
| `charts/` | `useExpenseCharts`, `useBudgetCharts`, `useReportCharts` |
| `reports/` | `useExpenseReportApiData`, `useExpenseReportsPageController`, etc. |
| `flow/` | Flow/dashboard orchestration for a feature |
| `settings/` | Feature-scoped settings hooks |

Rules:

- When a feature has **many hooks** or a **clear split** (e.g. half are report-only), introduce subfolders instead of a flat `hooks/` directory.
- Imports should use **`@/features/{name}/hooks/...`** so path depth stays stable when files move.
- **Admin** and other nested feature roots (`system/admin/`) follow the same pattern: `admin/pages/`, `admin/components/`, `admin/hooks/`, `admin/utils/` with the same subfolder rules.

### `utils/` and `constants/`

- Pure functions, mappers, and non-React state builders live in `utils/` (with subfolders if needed).
- Shared default objects and static keys live in `constants/` or `config/` as already used.

## Naming

| Artifact | Convention | Example |
|----------|------------|---------|
| React components | PascalCase `.jsx` | `ExpenseReportHeader.jsx` |
| Hooks | `use` + PascalCase, camelCase file | `useExpenseForm.js` |
| Domain | `{entity}.{role}.js` | `expense.transformers.js` |
| Redux | `{slice}.actions.js`, `.reducer.js`, `.actionTypes.js` | `expenses.actions.js` |
| Config | `*Config.js` or `constants/` | `expenseConfig.js` |

## Imports

- Use `@/` path alias for all app imports (`@/shared/...`, `@/features/...`, `@/config/...`).
- Prefer `@/features/{name}/...` over long relative chains (`../../..`) inside features so moves between subfolders do not churn imports.

## Barrel exports

- Feature root `components/index.js` (and optionally `hooks/index.js` when used) should aggregate public exports with `export * from "./{subfolder}/..."` or explicit names.
- **Concern subfolders** may expose `index.js` when multiple modules are exported from that folder; otherwise import directly from the file path.
- Prefer importing from feature barrels when the feature exports a stable API to the rest of the app.

## New top-level `src/` directories

Do not add new roots under `src/` without an ADR and alignment with `docs/adr/` patterns.

## References

- Config entry: `src/config/index.js`
- Route catalog: `src/app/routing/routeCatalog.js`
- Redux store: `src/redux/store.js`
